---
const { contactEmail } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="legal-content">
  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Overview</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains how Restart Apps ("we", "us", or "our") handles information when
      you use the NYC Jobs mobile application, listed in some stores as NYC Government Job Tracker
      (the "App" or "Service").
    </p>
    <p>
      The App helps users search NYC government job listings, save jobs, save search filters, create
      local job alerts, and optionally sign in with Google or Apple to personalize the experience.
      The App is not an official City of New York application and is not affiliated with, endorsed
      by, or sponsored by the City of New York.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    <h3>Information you choose to store in the App</h3>
    <p>
      The App stores certain information locally on your device so features can work properly. This
      can include saved searches, saved jobs, the application status and notes you add to saved
      jobs, filter selections, onboarding state, job alert preferences, reminder settings, and alert
      match activity.
    </p>
    <h3>Account sign-in and Firebase</h3>
    <p>
      If you choose to sign in, the App uses Google Sign-In or Sign in with Apple with Firebase
      Authentication. Through that process, your sign-in provider and Firebase may provide us access
      to basic account information associated with your account, such as your display name, email
      address, profile photo where available, and authentication identifiers needed to keep you
      signed in.
    </p>
    <p>
      When you are signed in, the App may use Firebase Cloud Firestore to sync your saved jobs, the
      application status and notes you add to them, saved search history, filter selections, job
      alert preferences, reminder settings, and related app settings so you can continue using those
      features across devices.
    </p>
    <h3>Job search and alert activity</h3>
    <p>
      When you search for jobs, apply filters, open job details, or create alerts, the App sends the
      related search parameters to NYC Open Data so matching job listings can be returned. Alert
      schedules and related filter settings are stored locally on your device and, if you are signed
      in, may also be synced with Firebase Cloud Firestore.
    </p>
    <h3>Permissions</h3>
    <p>
      Notifications: If you grant notification permission, the App can send local job alert
      notifications to your device.
    </p>
    <p>
      Approximate location: The App may request approximate location permission only when you choose
      to use current-location job search features. Your device's geocoding service (Google on
      Android, Apple on iOS) turns it into a place name to fill in the search; it is not sent to our
      servers.
    </p>
    <p>
      Calendar: If you choose Add to Calendar on a job, the App opens your device's calendar with
      the job's title and closing date filled in so you can save the event. The App does not read
      your calendar.
    </p>
    <h3>Analytics, diagnostics, and performance</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, and Firebase Performance Monitoring to
      understand app usage, diagnose crashes, and improve reliability and performance. This can
      include device and app information, interaction events, crash traces, and performance data. It
      does not include your search text, your notes, or your account identifiers. Where the law
      requires approval, nothing is collected until you allow it. You can turn analytics and crash
      reports off separately in Settings at any time; performance data follows the analytics
      setting.
    </p>
    <h3>App integrity and Insights data</h3>
    <p>
      The App uses Firebase App Check, with Google Play Integrity on Android and Apple App Attest on
      iOS, to confirm requests to our Firebase services come from a genuine copy of the App. Hiring
      Insights figures are prepared from NYC Open Data and downloaded from Firebase Cloud Storage;
      those requests include standard network information such as your IP address.
    </p>
    <h3>Advertising and Google AdMob</h3>
    <p>
      The App may include advertising features through Google AdMob. If a version of the App
      includes AdMob, Google and its partners may automatically collect information such as your
      advertising ID, device identifiers, IP address, approximate location, device and operating
      system details, and ad interaction data in order to serve, measure, and improve ads.
    </p>
    <p>
      Depending on your region and the App configuration, ads may be personalized or
      non-personalized, and you may be shown a consent message before ads are requested. For more
      information about how Google handles data, review Google's Privacy Policy: <a
      href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener
      noreferrer">https://policies.google.com/privacy</a>
    </p>
    <h3>Purchases and NYCJobs Pro</h3>
    <p>
      If you buy or restore the one-time NYCJobs Pro upgrade, Google Play or Apple's App Store
      processes the transaction under its own terms and privacy policy. The App receives purchase
      and entitlement information needed to complete, verify, restore, and remember the upgrade. We
      do not receive your full payment-card details. A Pro entitlement flag is also stored on your
      device.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
    <p>
      We use information handled by the App to retrieve and display job listings and job details
      from NYC Open Data; save your jobs, searches, and filter preferences on your device; sync
      saved jobs, saved search history, alert preferences, and related settings across your
      signed-in devices; create and deliver local job alert notifications; let you sign in with
      Google or Apple and show your profile information in the App; measure app usage, diagnose
      crashes, and monitor performance; process and restore the NYCJobs Pro entitlement through the
      applicable app store; respond to support, privacy, and data deletion requests; and, if ads are
      enabled, support advertising, consent handling, ad measurement, and fraud prevention through
      Google AdMob and related Google services.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Data Sharing and Third Parties</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The App relies on third-party services and public data providers that may process data in
      accordance with their own terms and privacy policies, including NYC Open Data; Google Sign-In,
      Sign in with Apple, and Firebase Authentication, if you choose to sign in; Firebase Cloud
      Firestore, if you choose to use signed-in sync; Firebase Analytics, Firebase Crashlytics, and
      Firebase Performance Monitoring; Firebase App Check with Google Play Integrity or Apple App
      Attest, and Firebase Cloud Storage for Insights data; Google Maps on Android, Apple Maps on
      iOS, and the geocoding, device-location, and platform services used for maps and optional
      location-aware search; Google AdMob and related Google advertising or consent tools, if
      advertising is enabled; and Google Play Billing or Apple StoreKit and the applicable app store
      when you purchase or restore NYCJobs Pro.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Data Storage and Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Saved jobs, search history, filters, onboarding status, alert settings, reminder settings, and
      alert match activity are stored locally on your device until you remove them, clear app data,
      or uninstall the App.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you sign in with Google or Apple, your authentication state is managed through your sign-in
      provider and Firebase and may persist until you sign out. While signed in, saved jobs, their
      application status and notes, saved search history, filter selections, job alert preferences,
      reminder settings, and related app settings may also be stored in Firebase Cloud Firestore
      under your Firebase Authentication user ID until you remove them in the App or delete your
      account.
    </p>
    <p>
      Signing out stops syncing and removes that account's library from the device, but it does not
      delete synced data already stored in Firebase.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics, advertising, diagnostic, performance, transaction, and app-store records are
      retained according to our service configuration, operational needs, legal obligations, and the
      retention practices of the applicable third-party provider. Account deletion does not cancel
      or erase purchase records maintained by Google Play or Apple.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Data Deletion Requests</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your signed-in account from Settings in the App. Account deletion removes your
      Firebase Authentication account and synced App data stored in Firebase, such as synced saved
      jobs and their notes, search history, alert preferences, and related settings.
    </p>
    <p>
      You may also contact us at <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a> with deletion
      questions. Some data handled by third-party services may remain subject to those services' own
      retention and deletion practices.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can remove local data on your device by deleting saved content in the App, clearing the
      App's data from your device settings where available, or uninstalling the App.
    </p>
    <p>
      Instructions for deleting your account, including without the App, are on the
      <a href="/apps/nyc-government-jobs/delete-account">account deletion page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Data Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use commercially reasonable measures provided by your device's platform and the third-party
      services we rely on. However, no method of transmission over the Internet or electronic
      storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      The App is not directed to children under 13, and we do not knowingly collect personal
      information from children under 13.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Your Choices</h2>
    <p>
      You may use the App without signing in. You can sign out to stop future account-based syncing
      on that device; deny or revoke notification and approximate-location permissions in device
      settings; manage advertising consent through the privacy options shown in the App where
      available; remove saved content using in-app controls; and delete your signed-in account and
      synced App data from Settings.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>External Services and Official Sources</h2>
    <p>
      NYC government job listings and related details shown in the App are sourced from NYC Open
      Data. Official information and application actions should be verified through CityJobs: <a
      href="https://cityjobs.nyc.gov/jobs" target="_blank" rel="noopener
      noreferrer">https://cityjobs.nyc.gov/jobs</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Changes to This Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. When we do, we will update the effective
      date shown above. Your continued use of the App after changes become effective means you
      accept the updated policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-block" data-reveal>
    <h2>Contact Us</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions about this Privacy Policy, contact us at: <a
      href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`}>{contactEmail}</a>
    </p>
  </section>
</div>
